          "worked": "Subtracting whole equations preserves equality. Subtract the first equation from the second to eliminate $y$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(3x-y)-(2x-y)&=4-(-3)\\\\x&=7\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute $x=7$ into the first equation.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2(7)-y&=-3\\\\-y&=-17\\\\y&=17\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck both original equations:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2(7)-17&=-3\\\\3(7)-17&=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $x=7$ and $y=17$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
