          "worked": "Subtracting whole equations preserves equality. Subtract the second equation from the first to eliminate $x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(4x+3y)-(4x+2y)&=10-5\\\\y&=5\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute $y=5$ into the second equation.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4x+2(5)&=5\\\\4x&=-5\\\\x&=-\\frac54\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck both original equations:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4\\left(-\\frac54\\right)+3(5)&=10\\\\4\\left(-\\frac54\\right)+2(5)&=5\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $x=-\\frac54$ and $y=5$.",
